Track 1: Mylar Ribbon Swallows the Spark
- Story & Context: When bootleg power tapped from the accelerator’s dead cooling matrix surged during the club's opening night, blue electrical fire leaped across the concrete, threatening to fry the PA until Elder Kwak blasted a 35-Hz tuba drone that miraculously absorbed the line's feedback buzz. As the spliced reels caught the scent of scorched iron and burning reel tape, Minnie calmed the panicked room by leaning into her ribbon mic and singing, "Hold the rim and count to four, the copper's coming alive." The seventy dancers in the tunnel froze, caught between terror and euphoria, before Sean dropped a devastating, low-passed drum break that set the whole concrete ring swaying.
