- Story & Context: Tucked into the accelerator’s dead target chamber with a cracked thermos of barley tea, Minnie penned this confessional after her Seoul management company formally canceled her contract for refusing to bleach her hair and sing over quantized euro-pop. Between the soft hiss of peeling adhesive tape and Kwak warming his brass mouthpiece with short, sleepy puffs of air, she recorded her multi-layered harmonies straight into a dying cassette recorder, declaring: "Take your plastic trophy back, my frequency runs in the dirt." The track leaked across regional radio when an engineering student played the bootleg master over the university PA, launching the entire Daejeon subculture overnight.
