Track 3: Chroma-Lag in the Gweodo Ring
- Story & Context: By the autumn municipal raids, local lore held that the subterranean concrete had absorbed so much brass vibration that the circular tunnel generated its own warm acoustic decay even when the generators were shut down. When municipal officers breached the blast doors expecting an illegal isotope lab, the acrid stench of their flares only revealed two hundred kids resting on velvet cushions while Kwak sustained a final, beautiful, subterranean tuba tone beneath Minnie's fading vocal loops: "We spun the heavy particles until they turned to silk." The police simply stood listening as the sound rolled around the ring, unable to find an electronic power source to disconnect.
